    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="37827e22-b574-5add-847a-e3384c526254" activityNameId="6a24db1a-d3fa-5d95-8ed9-210cb0c3298e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at wind farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at wind farm
UUID=b35b43a0-cf11-3cf1-ba91-54faaf294f6c
Electricity mix from wind power in Europe.
The mix consists of 87% from onshore wind farms and 13% from offshore wind farms, reflecting a total electrictiy generation of 420 TWh from onshore wind farms and 61.8 TWh from offshore wind farms in 2024 (source: ENTSO-E).

The considered contributions from different wind turbine sizes to the electrcity generation mix are:
50% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &lt; 3 MW (modelled using 2.3 MW onshore wind turbine)
22% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 3 MW and &lt; 4 MW (modelled using 3.4 MW onshore wind turbines)
10% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 4 MW and  &lt; 5.5 MW (modelled with 4.5 MW onshore wind turbines)
5% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 5.5 MW (modelled with 6.4 MW onshore wind turbines)
5% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &lt; 7 MW (modelled with 5 MW offshore wind turbines)
7% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 7 MW  and &lt; 12 MW (modelled with 10 MW offshore wind turbines)
1% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 12 MW (modelled with 15 MW offshore wind turbines)

Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b35b43a0-cf11-3cf1-ba91-54faaf294f6c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
